From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: add a bounded O82 bonded video AVR experiment

Use the standard atomic VRR_ENABLED request with one logical encoder owner.
Validate both DSI hosts and local INTF periods before enabling
continuous AVR.
The read-only opt-in parameter defaults to zero. The exact PB/42 OEM
120 Hz profile admits at most 32 additional lines. No qualified connector
range or vrr_capable claim is supplied.

Based on PortareOS continuous video AVR operations, patch 1097 at
67ed458421d919aba9c687c3f72d7678954b6902, and the Uke OEM QSync contract:
MiCode/vendor_opensource_display-drivers at
44275c404a677d9d9e5230fedd1af2ef02fc7b9a.
Retain upstream Linux GPL-2.0-only licensing and existing file attribution.
No panel commands or donor panel range are imported.

Link: https://github.com/portare-ch/portareos/blob/67ed458421d919aba9c687c3f72d7678954b6902/projects/PortareOS/devices/SM8550/patches/linux/1097-drm-msm-dpu-AVR-variable-refresh-on-DSI-video-mode.patch
Signed-off-by: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
